109	1_Company_Policies.pdf	6	y void insurance coverage.\nPage 4 of 9\nPremier Logistics — Company Policies\n4. Warehouse & Inventory Policy\n4.1 Receiving Goods\n● All incoming goods m\ny void insurance coverage.\nPage 4 of 9\nPremier Logistics — Company Policies\n4. Warehouse & Inventory Policy\n4.1 Receiving Goods\n● All incoming goods must be logged as a warehouse receipt at the time of physical entry, recording the entry \ndate, warehouse location, and an itemized packing list.\n● Goods are not considered "in Company custody" until a warehouse receipt has been generated and \nconfirmed.\n4.2 Storage Status & Duration\n● Warehouse receipts are tracked as Stored, Released, or In Transit. Storage status must reflect the physical \nlocation of the goods at all times.\n● Standard free storage duration and applicable storage/demurrage charges beyond that period are set out \nin the Company Rules document (Section 7).\n4.3 Stock Integrity\n● Any discrepancy between recorded inventory and physical stock (shortage, damage, misplacement) must \nbe reported to a Warehouse Supervisor the same 	[-0.010273055,0.024429524,0.02114531,-0.03844326,0.015904663,0.0066718697,-0.0061942977,-0.014710743,-0.009335795,-0.013578384,0.0057358807,-0.017830495,-0.0023180582,-0.011823897,0.11568196,-0.0007877866,0.016809305,-0.000981616,0.0013856554,-0.0026730234,0.0014563786,0.007231734,0.009938859,-0.015803507,0.006519962,0.004125283,0.03032915,5.6910383e-05,0.04827536,0.002704284,-0.013329146,-0.0019426855,0.011336633,0.016684866,-0.0028089208,0.02296919,-0.0061611617,-0.0039990875,-0.017270833,0.0028126475,-0.02532879,0.035063896,0.0018490859,-0.00682567,-0.029610883,0.003988772,0.013683227,-0.014320698,-0.0012199889,0.0069404063,0.0016500426,-0.018770248,-0.017160103,-0.19323598,0.013465502,-0.016361902,-0.0031554713,0.004695629,0.0059600733,-0.013440253,-0.011399612,0.024617655,0.008259077,0.0042153024,-0.0022985905,-0.0010780029,-0.00582847,-0.0029184169,-0.0042617917,-0.0025606265,0.