110	1_Company_Policies.pdf	7	● Any discrepancy between recorded inventory and physical stock (shortage, damage, misplacement) must \nbe reported to a Warehouse Supervisor the same \n● Any discrepancy between recorded inventory and physical stock (shortage, damage, misplacement) must \nbe reported to a Warehouse Supervisor the same day it is discovered and logged as an incident.\n5. Cargo Release Policy\n5.1 Authorization Requirement\n● Cargo may leave warehouse custody only after a cargo release record has been created and formally \nauthorized by a designated employee. No goods are released on verbal instruction alone.\n● Release authorization requires verification of the carrier or consignee identity (name, and where \napplicable, driver license number and PRO/tracking number) before goods are handed over.\n5.2 Release States\n● Cargo release records move through Pending → Approved → Released. Goods must not be handed over \nwhile a release is in Pending status.\n● A release is only considered complete once the release_date and recipient details are recorded in the \nsystem.\n	[-0.0071011414,0.015119862,0.009716423,-0.038611043,0.024029452,0.00072414574,-0.0055086203,0.015887767,-0.005642634,3.3404827e-05,0.004168544,-0.009922681,0.003832874,-0.0027338634,0.11450365,-0.0037358382,0.025352705,0.005560221,-0.013582981,0.00017031454,-0.0017250722,-0.007102878,-0.013217129,-0.02867727,0.009263291,0.005444006,0.0069782753,0.0062118853,0.04324862,0.00297446,-0.01519225,0.010798042,-0.0011933007,0.013664228,0.000111387686,0.0071794325,-0.0045254217,-0.0024338446,-0.004801781,0.0011674371,-0.025190085,0.030906258,0.0046309885,0.0057144663,-0.025563518,-0.008124146,0.010822002,-0.009714574,-0.002780417,-0.004545666,-0.00018992138,-0.018879887,-0.0073932842,-0.22090054,-0.004727182,-0.017684143,-0.009738602,0.005450158,-0.0037003057,-0.0061915815,-0.005674018,0.014262004,0.014642594,0.01179872,0.00053407496,-0.007972619,0.0021792797,-0.01104464,-0.028702732,-0.022939451,-0.