120	2_Standard_Operating_Procedures.pdf	2	nual and the Code of \nConduct. Where a step requires a system entry, that entry is the official record — work is not considered complete \nuntil the co\nnual and the Code of \nConduct. Where a step requires a system entry, that entry is the official record — work is not considered complete \nuntil the corresponding system record is updated.\n2. SOP — Customer Onboarding & Account Creation\nTrigger: A new customer requests to open an account or book their first shipment.\nResponsible Role: Sales / Customer Onboarding staff.\nSteps: \n1. Collect company name, contact person, email, phone number, and address.\n2. Verify the customer is not already registered under an existing customer_code to avoid duplicate accounts.\n3. Create the account with status Active and generate a unique customer_code.\n4. Confirm account creation to the customer with their reference code.\n5. Log the creation date; the account is now eligible to receive quotations and book shipments.\nRecords Updated: customers table (new record, status = Active).\n3. SOP — Shipment Booking\nT	[-0.00827409,0.015750205,0.016488366,-0.054346506,0.0021843195,-0.0008227277,0.004580348,-0.007050979,-0.027448524,-0.010499152,-0.009625729,-0.011959442,-0.003803786,0.011849773,0.113542736,0.0042821877,0.0063336133,0.024511503,-0.0091659995,-0.022816785,-0.009033708,0.0053474507,-0.015691567,-0.009546342,0.0016565485,0.0064006797,-0.008976088,0.0074415053,0.019883903,-0.0021235917,-0.001570865,-0.007793981,0.0020727734,0.008405199,-0.006563087,0.027606443,-0.019222733,0.0061205355,-0.018046217,0.003203858,0.0036370063,0.029490016,-0.014720755,-0.0029501407,-0.008279593,-0.0073355054,0.012064658,-0.036793172,-0.014216779,-0.0046091056,0.0023480658,-0.017329117,-0.018022047,-0.21089377,-0.014865642,-0.03372166,0.001123585,-0.016726807,0.0066855103,-0.011031607,-0.007943234,0.028219907,-0.035746343,0.008387829,-0.01964437,-0.010939738,0.014104309,0.0066183656,-0.009157107,-0.00